<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moravian Gate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moravian Gate is a lowland corridor in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudetes">Sudetes</a>, linking the valley of the Oder with that of the Bečva, a tributary of the Morava. It has been a natural route between the Baltic and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> basin since prehistoric times, used by the Amber Road and later by major roads and railways.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moravian-gate.jpg" alt="Moravian Gate" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Radim Holiš · CC BY-SA 3.0 cz · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C3%BDhled_z_hradu_Star%C3%BD_Ji%C4%8D%C3%ADn_(01).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
